WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.540
He's confessing!

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.140
Katou's definitely being confessed to!

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.740
Hey!

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.420
I found them first.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.060
B-But!

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:11.570
But!

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:17.010
Wanting to have the girl all for yourself the very moment a rival appears...

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.540
...gives you tons of lousy main character points!

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:26.120
If you say anything like "This made me finally realise that I...",

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.960
you'll get twice the loser points!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.370
Sorry, but I can't hear what they're saying,

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:32.300
so could you perhaps shut up for good?

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.810
Congratulations on joining the lousy main character hall of fame, Morals-kun.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.030
Here's your reward.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.140
I'm sorry!

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.900
I may be lousy,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.950
but I'm not a masochist, so could you please stop?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.210
And anyway,

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.530
Katou-san's looks have been all right from the get-go.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.660
She just doesn't stand out at all, to a lethal extent.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.820
That latest one really was lethal.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:03.200
But lately, thanks to my acting guidance and Sawamura-san's styling,

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.620
she's been getting increasingly polished as a main heroine.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.090
There's no way a male student or two wouldn't react to that.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:17.700
I wanted to have her shocking high school début coincide with the release of our game at winter Comiket.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.590
But things had progressed this much without me even noticing?

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.090
Um, sorry,

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:28.100
but having my private matters spied on and talked about so casually is quite problematic for me.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.770
So, why did you turn him down?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:35.580
You have to do suspicious things which others can easily misunderstand,

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.110
or this lousy main character will get conceited.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.800
But if I start going out with someone,

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.250
I will be busy with dates and such on weekends.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.620
And what about that?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.000
We're approaching our development deadline.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.370
I don't have time for that, do I?

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:56.840
Scripting, debugging, organising the printing, preparing for the event...

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:01.450
I can't think about anything but the circle before winter Comiket.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.320
K-Katou!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.340
I see!

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.600
Katou-san.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:12.600
I now understand very well just how strongly you feel about making this game.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.350
However.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.520
Unless the art is finished by our development deadline,

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.860
winter Comiket and everything else will be nothing but a pipe dream.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.770
Did the writer and director who not only stalled the scenario...

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:27.810
...but increased the amount of art needed by adding new routes say something?

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.830
I am terribly sorry!

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:34.540
But it's late even based on the schedule we already extended.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.320
According to the schedule,

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.140
it'd be high time for you to be done, even with the added work.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.500
But...

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.550
I couldn't come up with any main heroine-like ideas until recently.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.670
Ah, I am terribly sorry.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:49.810
Is that all?

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.100
What are you trying to say?

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:58.190
I feel like you're obsessing over quality so much that you're not getting anywhere.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.760
Are you saying I'm working hard for nothing?

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:02.340
I wouldn't go that far.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.320
However, the improvement doesn't seem to be in proportion to the time spent.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.830
What do you know-

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.720
Do you think I don't?

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.050
I always-

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.180
Wait a minute!

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.370
If you have any complaints, tell me, the director!

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.210
Eriri will be fine!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.590
Even though it's her first time doing game art?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.300
Even though she's never completed one before?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.890
Regardless of that, Eriri has great achievements with doujinshi!

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.220
Tomoya!

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.400
She's never dropped one before!

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.640
She steadily finished every book!

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:39.310
She's a superior creator who draws exactly what she's envisioned!

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.230
Are you trying to praise her?

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.360
Got it, I'll do it properly!

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.000
Don't worry!

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.660
No matter what it is, I'll finish it in time!

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.290
Okay?

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.210
So I'm waiting on material for the rest?

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.420
Bleh!

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.600
N-Nasu Highlands?

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.680
Yeah, our villa.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.760
I thought I'd let you know before I leave.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.390
You've been there once before.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.830
The one where we went when we were in the second year of primary school?

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:16.980
That's right.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:20.150
I thought I'd hole up there alone.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.940
Until when?

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:26.740
The deadline for me to deliver the final versions was extended until next weekend, wasn't it?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.940
You're going to drag it out until then?

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.820
In exchange, I'll be sure to finish it on time.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.980
Believe in me!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:38.250
I've believed in you the whole time, and yet we're in this situation!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.620
It'll be fine this time!

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.920
I won't leave the villa before I'm done drawing everything!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:44.940
And anyway,

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.060
what about school?

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.960
I have to skip it or I won't make it.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:55.680
Why are you in such a tight spot this time anyway?

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.360
At your normal speed, if you worked at it seriously...

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:06.400
This time, I can't lose, no matter what.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.150
Eriri...

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.780
All right, I'm going now.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:15.740
I'll contact you!

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:18.330
I'll definitely e-mail you every day!

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.710
So wait for me!

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:28.460
Got it, I'll wait.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.190
Sure!

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:32.800
Eriri!

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:34.920
What?

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.460
You will come back, right?

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.350
You won't disappear or anything, will you?

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.780
Of course!

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.490
What are you saying, Tomoya?

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:44.190
Uh, I guess, but...

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:45.870
You're weird.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.550
Ah!

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.620
She will not return!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.200
She will disappear!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.650
Stop feeding my anxiety!

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:02.210
But being all alone deep in the mountains in the middle of nowhere...

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.620
Will she be all right?

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.080
I'm sure she will!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.070
I've been there once before.

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.100
There's even a convenience store close by.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.280
That's not the issue.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.330
Huh?

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:17.850
Letting a creator free right before her deadline...

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.850
You the director just made a fatal mistake.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.530
B-But Eriri said she won't make it otherwise...

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.360
You're too naive, Morals-kun.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.180
That judgement of yours was...

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.610
Stop, stop, stop!
extremely naive!

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.040
See?

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.890
She contacted me yesterday like she said she would,

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.870
and she got two drawings done on the first day.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.900
Huh, it's progressing well.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:41.750
Right?

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.850
There's still a week left, so she has plenty of time!

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:46.150
That's what it's always like at first.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:46.960
Huh?

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:50.760
I heard this from a certain editor...

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.590
You aren't close to any editors apart from Machida-san, are you, Utaha-senpai?

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:58.680
Creators running away follow a particular pattern.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.280
What?

00:08:59.280 --> 00:08:59.930
A ghost story?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.000
So Morals-kun, you'd better be careful too.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.440
Pattern?

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.200
First, level one.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.940
They start speaking more harshly.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.440
Ah, I see.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:12.610
Then, level two.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.750
They blame themselves.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.080
O-Okay.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.950
After that, level three.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.260
They start answering later and later.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.890
Next, level four.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.490
"I want to die!", or "I can't take it any more!",

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:28.430
they will wallow in self-pity without any consideration for others.

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:29.340
Whoa.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:31.830
And finally, level five.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:35.340
One day, you can't contact them any more.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.630
By the way, on level six,

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.440
even if you go looking for the female creator who disappeared,

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.280
apparently it's common that she's got a new pen name and a new guy, and is working a completely new job.

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:52.510
So consequently the cast-aside man doesn't need to worry about it, is what Machida-san had to say.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:54.940
I'm sorry, was that last one necessary?

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:56.150
Anyway,

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:59.460
if you start noticing this pattern in Sawamura-san's e-mails,

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:00.900
take note of it.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:03.200
Ah.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:10.370
So, how long is she going to hole up there?

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:14.210
The deadline for the final version is Monday morning, so...

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:17.700
So, Aki-kun,

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:21.390
how about we go to Nasu Highlands on Saturday to pick Eriri up,

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:27.330
stay a night at the villa and go home together on Sunday?

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:32.480
Katou, do you understand that you're suggesting a trip with one guy and two girls?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.550
Considering that we've done overnight stays with one guy and four girls,

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:39.420
I wonder what I should think about this circle.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:42.500
I can't this time.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.040
I have to do things for the final version too.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.620
Ah, I see.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.620
So I can't either.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.120
I have to help you.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:52.430
Sorry, and thanks for that.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:54.900
I'm free the whole weekend,

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.960
so if necessary, just contact me.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.880
Yeah, thanks.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:07.270
Considering that week by week, different girls spend the night in the guy's room,

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:10.180
I wonder what I should think about this circle.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:14.110
<i>I sent you what I got done today.</i>

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:14.960
Sure.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.030
Just one?!

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:21.660
<i>Sorry, I can't quite understand what you're asking, so could you please say it again?</i>

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:22.680
It's great!

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:26.290
You've done your best illustration yet, Kashiwagi Eri-sensei!

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:31.540
<i>Anyway, with this, the Ruri route is done.</i>

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.650
<i>I'm currently working on the grand route you wrote.</i>

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.420
I see?

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.340
Finally?

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.290
<i>I knew it already,</i>

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.300
<i>but it has a completely different feel from the earlier scenarios.</i>

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:45.400
W-Well, the writer is different, to begin with.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:49.520
<i>I think it needs a slightly different approach with both the line art and the colouring.</i>

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.900
<i>So I think the progress may be just a little bit slower from tomorrow on.</i>

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.940
What, it'll be even slower than now?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.230
<i>Sorry, I can't quite understand what you're asking, so could you please say it again?</i>

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:04.630
Sensei, I will wait however long it takes for you to draw something you find acceptable!

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.370
I've told you to swallow before speaking!

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.370
I told you, didn't I, Morals-kun?

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:20.050
That leaving Sawamura-san alone was a fatal mistake.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:23.350
But Eriri has never dropped her work before-

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.480
Level one.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:26.680
They start speaking more harshly.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:32.090
She will probably move to level two by tonight, so be prepared.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:34.890
She still drew yesterday.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.400
Even if it was just one illustration.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.860
An artist stops drawing in an instant.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:44.130
And you can't know when they can draw again.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.990
Sawamura-san said she'd change the style, right?

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:53.710
Taking on something new like that is the most dangerous time.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:57.120
Yes, I know it well.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:00.900
Ah, I can't come up with the plot for my new light novel!

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.870
I shouldn't have made it a school harem...

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:05.180
S-Senpai?

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:08.390
I should have made it a pure love story like before!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.280
I'm looking forward to your new series!

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:13.100
I will keep waiting, Kasumi Utako-sensei!

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.820
Eriri will be fine.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:20.970
She won't do anything reckless.

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:22.650
She's calculated it all properly.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:28.740
So I'm sure she'll finish it by the deadline with the current style.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:31.410
Morals-kun.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.980
Do you perhaps...

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:35.770
Yeah, I believe in her.

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:39.760
No, that's not faith.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.760
You simply don't expect anything.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:47.220
Do you think she has nowhere further to go as a creator?

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.300
I-I'm not saying that!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.690
It's just that-

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:53.600
Sawamura-san can't change her style,

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.020
or make any progress.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:58.370
Even when faced with a trial to overcome her bounds,

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.540
she backs off without taking it.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:02.490
That's what you are saying.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.930
What are you saying, Utaha-senpai?

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.780
Don't you want her to finish in time?

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:09.030
Morals-kun,

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.790
don't you want her to improve?

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.790
What's that?

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.420
It has nothing to do with me, but it still pisses me off.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:24.920
W-What does?

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.780
I, who supposedly dislikes Sawamura Eriri,

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:34.520
appreciates Kashiwagi Eri so much more than you, who supposedly understands her the best...

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.180
That messed-up reality.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.660
<i>Sorry, I made no progress today.</i>

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:54.040
<i>Honestly, I'm a bit lost.</i>

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:57.910
<i>I've been so closely involved with Kasumigaoka Utaha's scenario for the last half a year,</i>

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:01.980
<i>that I don't really know yet how I should approach your scenario.</i>

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:04.100
You're overthinking it.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.750
It's just my scenario.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:09.670
<i>You know, I actually tried drawing several illustrations.</i>

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.180
Huh?

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.080
<i>But I don't really feel any of them.</i>

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:17.060
<i>If they have the same touch as before, they feel out of place with the text...</i>

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.060
<i>So I threw all of them away.</i>

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.040
Don't do that.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.060
Wait a minute!

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:27.100
<i>Something like this hasn't happened before.</i>

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:29.070
<i>I'm not making any progress.</i>

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:31.600
<i>What happened to me?</i>

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.780
Try to do it more casually...

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:34.910
Like usual...

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.830
<i>But I'll be sure to make it in time!</i>

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.250
<i>I'll deal with my own failings by myself.</i>

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.380
No, it's not like you're failing...

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:43.370
<i>See you tomorrow.</i>

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:44.590
E-Eriri!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.180
I'm sorry, Tomo-kun...

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:59.730
I couldn't keep our promise...

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:01.480
I'm sorry.

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.940
So, any word from Eriri?

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.360
I see.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.690
Not to me, either.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:18.930
On the other hand, us contacting her wouldn't be good either.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:26.290
I wonder if we'll just have to take the grand route out.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:30.050
But that's the first scenario you've written, isn't it?

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:33.920
But the quality is so-so to begin with, right?

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:36.680
Leaving it out isn't going to have such a huge effect.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.930
I think Eriri wouldn't agree to it, though.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.630
Huh, why?

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.920
I was going to say something interesting,

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:53.530
but seeing your attitude, I don't feel like it any more.

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:56.200
Katou, haven't you been quite merciless to me lately?!

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.450
Well, however it is,

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:03.710
if something happens over the weekend, contact me right away.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:07.210
I'll even rush to Nasu Highlands.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:09.920
S-Sure, thanks.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.710
Still, I wonder if Eriri is all right.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.680
Is she eating properly?

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.440
She said cup yakisoba is her staple food.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:18.240
Sheesh.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.830
I hope she doesn't harm her health.

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:23.640
You sound like a mother, Katou.

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:26.620
I'm worried about things which worry me.

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:28.230
Has she caught a cold?

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:31.690
It's much colder there than in Tokyo, right?

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:36.790
Ah...

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:40.120
It was really cold nine years ago.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.210
Onii-chan?

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.980
Where did you go, Onii-chan?

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:09.980
Ruri is here.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:13.070
Where did you go, Onii-chan?

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:33.320
Eriri?

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.650
<i>There's snow, Tomoya!</i>

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:36.640
<i>It's so beautiful!</i>

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:37.870
W-What?

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:39.300
<i>Be that as it may,</i>

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.210
<i>it seems I'll be able to make the deadline!</i>

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.250
R-Really?

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:45.270
<i>I finally came up with a new way to draw it!</i>

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.550
<i>I can finally start working again!</i>

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:48.790
Huh?

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:49.450
Uh, wait a moment-

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:53.640
<i>You know, in a game, the characters and the background are normally drawn separately, right?</i>

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:59.040
<i>But when painting in the art club, the people
and scenery are presented in the same picture.</i>

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:01.930
<i>I felt there was something off about that difference.</i>

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.940
Wait, Eriri!

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.410
<i>What, Tomoya?</i>

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.620
You're changing the drawing style at this point?

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.380
<i>I'm changing everything!</i>

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.920
<i>First I paint it, then scan it, and after that-</i>

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.170
How many did you say you've done already?

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.720
<i>I'm only starting now!</i>

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.260
So five to go?

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.590
In one day?

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:22.250
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:24.080
<i>At least five!</i>

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.870
<i>But maybe even more once I get going!</i>

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:28.600
No, that's just not possible!

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:29.810
<i>I can do it!</i>

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:33.810
<i>Tomoya, as long as you expect it, I can do it.</i>

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:37.380
<i>I like the route you wrote.</i>

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:38.840
<i>I love it!</i>

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:42.600
<i>It's a happy end which has been shoehorned in,
ignoring all the foreshadowing,</i>

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:44.870
<i>but it made me feel really happy.</i>

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:47.230
<i>That's why I'll draw it.</i>

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:50.620
<i>No matter who says what, I'll finish all the art for it.</i>

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:53.110
Ruri, I'm here!

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:54.380
Here!

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.580
Onii-chan, where are we going?

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:00.740
Just come!

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:02.320
Seiji-kun, morning!

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:03.370
Morning, Meguri!

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:05.090
No! Run, Onii-chan!

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.500
Ruri! Ruri!

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:07.740
I will always...

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.510
Seiji-kun, I want to save Ruri!

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.640
Let's go back together,

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.610
Meguri, Ruri, and everybody.

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:14.510
Ruri.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.980
Thank you, Meguri.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:16.860
Seiji-kun.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:18.130
Onii-chan.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:19.380
We're home!

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:20.060
Meguri.

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:20.970
Ruri.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:21.970
Welcome home!

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:25.060
Hey, Ruri, you're clinging on to Seiji-kun too much!

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:27.260
What? Isn't it fine?

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:28.320
Right, Onii-chan?

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:29.450
Hey now!

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.040
Hey, you two...

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.270
Sheesh!

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:35.500
<i>No, I want you to tell me.</i>

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:38.510
<i>You can do it, of all people!</i>

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.850
<i>You really are amazing!</i>

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:42.090
<i>You are a genius!</i>

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:45.180
<i>So draw!</i>

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:47.550
You...

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:50.770
...should...

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.060
...just do what you want.

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:24.590
I did it.

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:27.220
I did it, Tomoya.

00:22:28.050 --> 00:22:30.910
I'm e-mailing all of it to you now.

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:32.230
<i>Hey, Eriri!</i>

00:22:32.230 --> 00:22:32.900
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:33.740
<i>Hang in there!</i>

00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:36.850
It's all right, Tomo-kun.

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:40.040
I'll be better tomorrow.

00:22:40.440 --> 00:22:44.400
So let's play games together, okay?

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:46.810
<i>Idiot!</i>

00:22:46.810 --> 00:22:48.300
<i>Wake up!</i>

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:49.570
<i>Eriri!</i>
